<topic id="GUID-92250AFC-BB37-44B6-8384-08372CED20B4" xml:lang="en-US"> 
  <title>Introduction</title> 
  <body> 
    <p>RZL-AX requires the BIOS to provide the MRC with an accurate MoP memory configuration prior to DRAM training. The primary sources for the MoP configuration are a BIOS knob, an on-board SPD, a 4-bit GPIO from the EC IO expander, or a 32-bit FPF fuse via CSME BUP-MKHI. Only the GPIO and FPF fuses are POR. 
    </p> 
    <table id="GUID-D878F9E9-27C1-40F5-9B86-2C36BA3C3AAF"> 
  <title> MoP FPF Configuration Format</title> 
  <tgroup cols="3"><colspec colnum="1" colname="col1" colwidth="*" /><colspec colnum="2" colname="col2" colwidth="*" /><colspec colnum="3" colname="col3" colwidth="*" /><thead> 
      <row> 
        <entry colname="col1"> Field 
        </entry> 
        <entry colname="col2"> Bit Range 
        </entry> 
        <entry colname="col3"> Description 
        </entry> 
      </row></thead> 
    <tbody> 
      <row> 
        <entry colname="col1"> Rank 
        </entry> 
        <entry colname="col2"> [0:0] 
        </entry> 
        <entry colname="col3"> 1R=0b; 2R=1b 
        </entry> 
      </row> 
      <row> 
        <entry colname="col1"> Die Density 
        </entry> 
        <entry colname="col2"> [3:1] 
        </entry> 
        <entry colname="col3"> 16Gb=010b; 24Gb=011b; 32Gb=100b 
        </entry> 
      </row> 
      <row> 
        <entry colname="col1"> Vendor 
        </entry> 
        <entry colname="col2"> [6:4] 
        </entry> 
        <entry colname="col3"> Micron*=001b; Samsung*=010b; SK Hynix*=011b 
        </entry> 
      </row> 
      <row> 
        <entry colname="col1"> Data Rate 
        </entry> 
        <entry colname="col2"> [9:7] 
        </entry> 
        <entry colname="col3"> 10.7 GT/s=001b; 9.6 GT/s=000b 
        </entry> 
      </row> 
      <row> 
        <entry colname="col1"> ECC 
        </entry> 
        <entry colname="col2"> [10:10] 
        </entry> 
        <entry colname="col3"> 0=Non-ECC; 1=OOBECC 
        </entry> 
      </row> 
      <row> 
        <entry colname="col1"> Reserved 
        </entry> 
        <entry colname="col2"> [31:11] 
        </entry> 
        <entry colname="col3"> 
        </entry> 
      </row> 
    </tbody> 
  </tgroup> 
  </table> 
  </body> 
